{
  "slug": "devflow",
  "name": "Devflow",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Structured AI development workflows for Claude Code. Enforces planning, approval, task tracking, and code review gates\nthrough MCP — so AI agents work within a defined process instead of writing code without oversight.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **7 commands** and **1 MCP server**.\n\n- **Commands** (7): `devflow-create` (Create a new flow with a one-line summary), `devflow-list` (List open flows as a Markdown table (⭐ marks own flows)), `devflow-next` (Show the next allowed action and step for the current flow), `devflow-review` (Submit the current flow for review (transitions to 'review' state)), `devflow-start` (Start a DevFlow session for a specific flow), `devflow-status` (Show the current DevFlow status (state, tasks, next step)), `devflow-tasks` (List tasks for the current DevFlow flow)\n- **MCP servers** (1): `devflow`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install devflow@claude-community` from `KlausFreiberufler/devflow-mcp`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "command": 7,
    "mcp": 1
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
  "author": {
    "name": "DevFlow",
    "url": "https://dev-flow.tech"
  },
